## Why Asked
Tests understanding of load balancer architecture choices and performance characteristics at scale

## Key Concepts
Event-driven vs epoll models, connection limits, HTTP vs TCP optimization, memory usage patterns, worker process management

## Code Example
```
# NGINX configuration
worker_processes auto;
events {
  worker_connections 10240;
}
http {
  upstream backend {
    server 10.0.0.1:80;
    server 10.0.0.2:80;
  }
}

# HAProxy configuration
global
  maxconn 1000000
defaults
  maxconn 50000
frontend http_front
  bind *:80
  default_backend servers
```

## Follow-up Questions
How do you handle SSL termination? What about health checks? How do you configure sticky sessions?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests fundamental REST API design, HTTP method understanding, and error handling - core skills for any API role at Meta.

## Expected Answer
Candidate should explain RESTful principles, proper HTTP status codes (200, 201, 400, 404, 500), and consistent JSON response format. Should mention validation and idempotency for PUT/DELETE.

## Code Example
```typescript
// Express.js example
app.get('/tasks', async (req, res) => {
  try {
    const tasks = await Task.findAll();
    res.json(tasks);
  } catch (error) {
    res.status(500).json({ error: 'Internal server error' });
  }
});
```
